        "entry_xTWgnb": {
          "type": "entry",
          "settings": {
            "full_width_enable": true,
            "title": "Maintenance",
            "text": "<p><strong>Maintenance Before and After Each Use</strong><br/><br/>1) Inspect the plug and the cord to ensure that it has not been damaged during operation or between uses. If the plug or cord is damaged, do not use the air mover and replace the damaged part immediately.<br/>2) Check the air intake and air discharge grills and make sure they are free of blockage.<br/><br/><strong>Cord Storage</strong><br/><br/>1) Before storing the air mover, ensure the on/off switch is turned to \"0\" OFF position, and unplug the unit from the power outlet.<br/>2) Wrap the power cord around the base of the handle.<br/>3) Use the attached power cable strap to hold the cord in place.<br/><br/><strong>Storing the Air Mover</strong><br/><br/>To conserve space while storing multiple units, this air mover can be stacked together with multiple additional units using the mounting pegs and inlets on each side of the unit.<br/><br/><strong>Replacing the Remote Control Battery</strong><br/><br/>NOTE: The remote control contains small parts. Be careful when replacing the battery and ensure all maintenance is completed on a flat and stable surface.<br/><br/>1) Locate the 3 screws on the rear of the remote control. Carefully remove these screws and keep them in a safe place.<br/>2) Remove the rear casing to access the battery. The battery and board can both be removed.<br/>3) Replace the battery with a suitable 27A 12V battery cell. Ensure the positive and negative battery connections are correctly positioned.<br/>4) Insert the board and battery back into the casing and secure in place by retightening the screws provided.</p>",
            "button_1_style": "white",
            "button_1_text": "",
            "button_1_url": "",
            "button_2_style": "white",
            "button_2_text": "",
            "button_2_url": "",
